tests/golden/check/success-clause-misuse.hero:17:41: error[success_without_end]: `when` says which result means `ob_peek` did what it was handed, and no parameter of it is marked `consumes`, `transfers` or `retains`: nothing here happens only on success
tests/golden/check/success-clause-misuse.hero:18:54: error[success_without_end]: `when` says which result means `ob_get` did what it was handed, and no parameter of it is marked `consumes`, `transfers` or `retains`: nothing here happens only on success
tests/golden/check/success-clause-misuse.hero:19:49: error[when_on_void]: `when` compares the result of `ob_take` with a value, and `ob_take` returns nothing: a call that cannot say whether it succeeded ends, transfers and retains unconditionally, so drop the clause
tests/golden/check/success-clause-misuse.hero:20:50: error[success_value_type]: `when true` compares the result of `ob_give` with a value of another type: the result is `i32`, and the clause takes an integer literal for an integer result and `true` or `false` for a `bool`
tests/golden/check/success-clause-misuse.hero:21:51: error[success_value_type]: `when 1` compares the result of `ob_test` with a value of another type: the result is `bool`, and the clause takes an integer literal for an integer result and `true` or `false` for a `bool`
tests/golden/check/success-clause-misuse.hero:22:22: error[one_mark_per_position]: `o` carries two of `consumes`, `transfers`, `acquires`, `retains` and `borrows`, and a value takes one: each says what the call does with the value's life, and a call does one thing with it
